**Last modified:** October 14, 2026 (the page also lists this as "Last updated"; it was first published March 9, 2021).

**Code example** (from the page's Usage section):

```jsx
import { useState } from 'react';
import { TextareaControl } from '@wordpress/components';

const MyTextareaControl = () => {
    const [ text, setText ] = useState( '' );

    return (
        <TextareaControl
            label="Text"
            help="Enter some text"
            value={ text }
            onChange={ ( value ) => setText( value ) }
        />
    );
};
```

**Props** (the page lists only these six):

- **`help`** (`string | Element`): Optional. Generates help text from the given content.
- **`hideLabelFromVision`** (`boolean`): Optional. When true, the label is visible only to screen readers.
- **`label`** (`string`): Optional. Generates a label from the given content.
- **`onChange`** (`(value: string) => void`): Required. Called with the new value each time the textarea changes.
- **`rows`** (`number`): Optional. Number of rows in the textarea. Default: 4.
- **`value`** (`string`): Required. The current value of the textarea.

The page also says that props not in this set are passed through to the textarea element.

**Not on the page:** The content does not include `__nextHasNoMarginBottom` or any deprecation notes, so I can't report them. The component's source README on GitHub, linked from the page, would be the place to check.

